$DATUM Method B: (for 2c): Glycoside 1c (0.37 g, 1.0 mmol) is dissolved in abs.
MeOH (10 mL), and treated wtih NaOH (0.135 g, 3.3 mmol) and NaBrO2 (0.094
g, 6.6 mmol). The solution is stirred and refluxed for 5 h. Subsequently
the mixture is cooled and treated with AcOH (0.5 mL). Workup as described
above gives unreacted 1c (6%) and the glycosides 2c. Yield 0.12 g, 31%.
mp(°C)b (solvent) 180-181 (EtOAc/Hx) [α ]D (c,CHCl3) ±21.3 (0.9)
