$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step- II: Preparation of 4-chloro 2-amino pyridine: Dissolved sodium
hydroxide in water (120 gm, 900 ml) and cooled to 0 to 5°C. Charged
Bromine (45 ml) slowly at 0°C and stirred for half hour. Charged
4-chloropyridine-2-carboxamide (60 gm) of at 0°C and stirred for 5
minutes. Heated the reaction mass to 100°C and maintained at reflux to
get clear solution. The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC.
After completion of the reaction, the reaction mass was cooled to 0 to
5°C in one hr, filtered the precipitated solid, washed with chilled
water, and dried at 50 to 55°C for 3 to 4 hrs. Dry wt: 28gm (Stage II).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hoffman degradation reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
